members.rationale:
The child map dates M2L0M under QOC (from 2020-10-23, open). All 4 mentions are named exactly 'NHS Shropshire, Telford and Wrekin Integrated Care Board', and every one is the procedure Buyer:
- 30808330 and 46737553: Community Ophthalmology, with the STW ICB also as review body;
- 46737574: Cataract/YAG, where SaTH, CHEC and SpaMedica are separate tenderer sections;
- 46822938: the joint NEPTS notice, as its own co-buyer.
No other body uses the code. The name is admitted only under QOC, and the head equals the mention name. Survivor 31542354 is a live PPON org.

Unit 1's 'no parent' was a failed fetch. The frozen child map has 03K under QOQ (RE5, from 2020-04-01, open), the row 'NHS HUMBER AND NORTH YORKSHIRE ICB - 03K'.

All 12 mentions:
- are named 'NHS Humber and North Yorkshire ICB';
- are the Buyer;
- come from the NECS NHSE1006 community dental MSP series (2024-10 to 2025-02), whose text says NECS works 'for and on behalf of NHS Humber and North Yorkshire ICB (HNY ICB) (the Relevant Authority)'.

NECS used 03K (North Lincolnshire's code) for all HNY lots (2, 3 and 4). That is HNY publishing under one of its own sub-ICB codes, not another body. The tenderers RJL and CHCP are separate sections. West Yorkshire's lot 1 sits separately under 03R. The name is admitted only under QOQ.

The child map dates D9Y0V under QRL (from 2020-10-23, open), with no other parent.

All 10 mentions are the Buyer, under two names: 'NHS Hampshire and Isle of Wight ICB' ×7 and 'NHS HAMPSHIRE AND THE ISLE OF WIGHT INTEGRATED CARE BOARD' ×3. They cover:
- the CYP complex domiciliary care framework (2023 to 2025);
- the Isle of Wight Place community beds series (2023 to 2024);
- the Barnardo's family support award (2022-12).

'Isle of Wight Place' appears only in titles, never as a party name. The suppliers are separate sections. Both names are admitted only under QRL. The Frimley D4U1Y holder is correctly a non-member here.

The child map dates D2P2L under QUA (from 2020-10-23, open).

All 16 mentions are the Buyer (2022-08 to 2026-05), and every name is Black Country ICB:
- 14 in mixed case;
- 1 in upper case;
- 1 typo, 'NHS Balck Country Integrated Care Board' (46978077, 2022-08-12, co-buyer with Dudley MBC, which is its own section).

The suppliers (GP practices M91013/M91019/M91616/M91647, charities, companies) are separate tenderer sections. The typo is the body's own misspelling, and the strict gate admits it only under QUA. The org is an identity loser, so it arms no name key. Survivor 31542353 is a live PPON org.
